		<title type="html"><![CDATA[100% guarantee non-interpenetration physics ?]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=170#p170"><![CDATA[
Even for ray cast wheels, a nonholonomic constraint is usually used, except that the lateral constraint force (friction) has a limited magnitude to allow for sliding. These constraints don't need special treatment if the engine can handle lo-hi limits on the Lagrange multipliers.<br><br>I'm guessing Doom3 uses Lagrange multipliers for bilateral constraints where penetration is not a conscern and impulses for contact to prevent penetration.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=12">Erin Catto</a> — Fri Jul 29, 2005 4:48 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
